    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "tonight is the Democratic nominee for President of the United States. Please welcome back to the late show Vice President Kamala Harris. Madam Vice President, thank you so much for being here again. It's so good to be with you. Always enjoyed talking to you on the show. Thank you. It's an honor to have the opportunity to do the show with you here tonight. One month from today is the election in November of everybody out there is registered and ready to vote. You got so much to get to. I don't never get to all the questions that I've got here. But before we do anything, I want to talk about the recovery. from Hurricane Helene and in the light of the fact that Hurricane Milton has strengthened once again to a category five hurricane and is headed for the West Coast of Florida. You were down in Georgia and North Carolina who are still in the midst of a massive cleanup and rescue and recovery efforts still. What do people need to know? Well, first of all, to all of those folks in North Carolina and Georgia, please know that FEMA and the people on the ground are there to help you. You are entitled to help. There's a lot of misinformation. And I beseech you. I beg you to please not pay attention to it, because there are a whole lot of folks who are there to give you help and aid in terms of the immediate aftermath and what people need to do in terms of getting through the height of this emergency and this crisis, but also in terms of long-term help. And that means applying for it knowing that the services are there. But I'll tell you Stephen, I mean,",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_09",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
